  "decision": "Select reviewed12.5 startup without tail wait for separate flash qualification; retain tail wait as a RAM diagnostic.",
  "limits": [
    "One observed RAM-awake trial per configuration; card ACMD41 duration and allocation scan position differ. Do not attribute total-cycle differences solely to startup optimization.",
    "The control ACMD41 interval is approximately204ms, versus approximately12ms in the startup trials; this dominates the apparent overall improvement.",
    "The selected optimization removes9ms of nominal initial clocks, about1ms of nominal divider settling and a duplicate SCR transaction under the fixed-board valid-supply assumption.",
    "The tail-enabled startup trial waited approximately10ms then used PIO. The no-tail trial begins PIO immediately; neither establishes an energy saving.",
    "Long exposure also enables preinitialization and twenty immediate LINE snapshots; it is a correctness/overlap diagnostic, not a like-for-like timing comparison.",
    "Times are400MHz RAM-counter intervals, not reset-release, power-good or onset-to-Standby measurements. No energy, cold-flash or reliability qualification is inferred.",
    "Markers do not provide an on-media checksum or establish arbitrary power-loss safety."
